Measured on this machine's real transcripts (520 agent-transcript JSONL files, 130 over 96 KB): a Swift re-implementation of exactly this loop costs 1.40-1.55 ms per file (best of 20), i.e. ~10.5 ms for 7 sessions per poll, ~30 ms for 20 poll-fresh sessions per poll. Parsing is unavoidable only for the records that can change the outcome: `lastMessageLine`, `lastTurnEndedLine`, `lastActivity`, `completionID`, `lastAssistantWasFinalText` are all overwritten by the newest matching record, and the 25 largest files average 67 records per tail. Vocabulary check over 120 real transcripts: every record has either `role` (user/assistant) or `type: turn_ended` — no unknown record kind needs to be looked at. A second filter is available free: the head's `unfinishedRunAt` is absent on 705 of 706 real main heads, and `inFlight` then depends only on `toolPending && modifiedAt` (lines 152-157).

